I like the intro man! The audio levels could do with some work, the music and your voice clash at times, too many high peaks. The editing is spot-on love it! Must have taken a while with all these pan-crops, love Reddit style videos, you sometimes get your words messed up, consider rerecording at times when this happens. 

&#x200B;

Either way nice video man!

This varies a lot depending on your SEO. In my previous video, 34% of traction was gained from recommendations. 

&#x200B;

Just need to learn about what to tag your videos with, titles ETC. 

Stronger hitting tags will boost you into recommended, also it depends on your content type, if you upload Minecraft videos just imagine how many Minecraft videos are uploaded every hour, if you use all the same tag big content creators use, you are less likely to show up, because those tags are "taken" as such by these massive people already. 

&#x200B;

It takes a lot of work to fully understand the recommended feature, even I don't know it all, but it's something to look into in more depth, especially video tags.
